ha_flic_buttons

This repository redistributes the "flic_button" integration from the Home
Assistant core pull request #182198 (https://github.com/home-assistant/core/pull/182198),
authored by Joost Lekkerkerker (@joostlek) and Shortcut Labs / 50ButtonsEach,
as a Home Assistant custom integration.

Original work: Copyright (c) Home Assistant contributors, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. See LICENSE.

Modifications by michis0806 (2026) are released under the same license and are
listed in CHANGELOG.md.

The runtime dependency pyflic-ble (https://github.com/50ButtonsEach/pyflic-ble)
is installed from PyPI. The local client.py adapts its connection initialization
from version 0.2.5; the Apache-2.0 license shipped with that version is included
as custom_components/flic_button/LICENSE.pyflic-ble.

The Flic 2 battery estimate uses the voltage/percentage curve published by
Shortcut Labs in flic2lib-android's BatteryLevel.java. See the source link in
sensor.py and README.md. No model-specific curve is assumed for other batteries.

